<title>SPAIN: Spain 97 budget deficit/gdp will be 3 pct-Rato.</title>
<headline>Spain 97 budget deficit/gdp will be 3 pct-Rato.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Spanish deficit will narrow to three percent of gross domestic product in the 1997 budget, while the debt to GDP level will decline, Economy Minister Rodrigo Rato said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;The public deficit will be at three percent and public debt will be declining,&quot; Rato told journalists at a news conference following cabinet approval of the 1997 budget draft.</p>
<p>The 1996 budget deficit to GDP is forecast at 4.4 percent.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
